promptVerbatim:
Create an original 1536×1024 true-transparent RGBA sprite sheet for JAMVERSE '96. Use the supplied Leo gameplay atlas only as identity and arcade-art reference; do not copy its poses. Draw exactly fifteen distinct, complete full-body Leo poses in a strict five-column by three-row grid, row-major, with generous gutters and outer margins. Keep long hair, fingers and shoes inside each cell. Consistent scale and camera, crisp readable arcade pixel clusters and strong dark outlines.

Leo is the pale aristocratic adult man and captain of the Blackthorn Court Kings. Preserve his pale skin, long wavy black hair, refined mustache, handsome composed face, natural adult human anatomy and controlled Victorian-gothic poise. He wears his tailored black basketball uniform with restrained crimson accents, matching shorts, dark legwear and red-black shoes. Exactly two arms, two hands, two legs and two shoes. No fangs, horns, cape, robe, monster traits, extra limbs, costume change or props.

This is a right-facing reverse dunk. Leo approaches image-right, turns his back and shoulders toward the imaginary rim, carries the separately rendered ball behind his crown in his right hand, then releases once backward through the rim. The basketball is separate game art and is never painted. Both hands remain visibly empty except for the implied live ball path; do not draw that ball. No sphere, ball, seams, court, hoop, rim, floor, ground shadow, background, glow, border, grid, text, teammate or opponent. The exterior and gutters must be genuine alpha-zero transparency, without checkerboard, matte, speckles or haze.

Fifteen sequential original poses with a readable backward carry and single release:
0: composed right-facing approach, eyes on the rim;
1: lengthens stride and lowers his center of gravity;
2: gathers the invisible ball beside his right hip and plants;
3: coils at the knees, right arm draws the ball path inward;
4: takeoff, shoulders begin turning away from the rim;
5: rises in a three-quarter back view, right elbow bent;
6: carries the invisible ball behind his head, hair flowing naturally;
7: reaches the apex with his back turned, right hand still behind the crown;
8: unwinds toward a profile while protecting the ball behind his head;
9: arches backward into the reverse finish, right arm begins extending behind him;
10 RELEASE at simulation tick21: right palm opens backward through the imaginary rim, fully empty; left arm balances;
11: empty right hand follows through behind him, no ball visible;
12: descends and rotates shoulders back toward image-right;
13: lands softly with knees flexed and complete shoes visible;
14: recovers to a composed right-facing ready stance.

Keep the motion distinct from a power, windmill, tomahawk, 360 or clutch dunk. Preserve Leo's pale face, long wavy black hair, refined mustache, human proportions and black/crimson kit in every pose. Keep the body readable through the turning poses. No ball in the artwork. Return only the transparent sprite sheet.
